e Black king on e8, forcing it to move (likely Kd7, Kf8, or Ke7 since Black hasn't castled). After the king moves, I capture the f7 pawn with my bishop, winning material and severely damaging Black's pawn structure around the king. This is a classic tactical blow that exploits the uncastled king and the weakness of f7.\n\nAnswer: B: c4-f7"}
