hop on f6 and threatens h7. Given that Black's king is on f8 and has already moved, the king position is compromised. The knight on g5 would create immediate tactical threats and force Black to deal with multiple problems. Black will likely have to move the bishop from f6, and my knight would dominate from g5, coordinating beautifully with my bishop on f7 to create a mating attack around the exposed king.\n\nAnswer: N: f3-g5"}
