ting threats.\n\n5. **N: b1-c3** - Solid development, supporting the center.\n\nReason:\nThe move **d5-d6** is the most forcing and positionally crushing. It:\n- Advances my passed pawn deep into Black's territory\n- Restricts Black's dark-squared bishop on f8\n- Cramps Black's entire position\n- Creates potential threats against the exposed king on e8\n- Forces Black to deal with the advanced pawn immediately\n\nThis pawn advance is thematic and strong in such positions where the opponent's king is still centralized.\n\nAnswer: P: d5-d6"}
