ces Black's King into a defensive position\n- Maintains the Rook's activity\n- Black cannot defend both pawns adequately\n- This creates immediate tactical pressure and likely wins material\n\nAfter Rd6, if the King moves to defend e6, I can capture on c6. If it defends c6, I capture on e6. The Black King cannot defend both pawns at once.\n\nAnswer: R: d7-d6"}
