d rook on a8! After the king moves, I can capture the rook on a8, winning significant material.\n\nReason: R: d6-d8 is clearly the best move because it:\n1. Gives check to the Black king on g6 (forcing it to move)\n2. After the king moves (likely to f7, h7, f5, or h5), I can capture the undefended rook on a8 with Rxd8\n3. This wins a full rook, giving me a decisive material advantage\n\nThis is a classic "check and win material" tactical pattern.\n\nAnswer: R: d6-d8'}
