* - Attacks the e4 pawn directly and cuts off Black's king from the 4th rank.\n\nReason: I choose **R: d8-g8** because it maintains maximum pressure on Black's position. This move:\n- Attacks the g7 pawn, forcing Black to defend\n- Keeps my rook on the dominant 8th rank\n- Restricts Black's king mobility\n- Maintains the initiative rather than playing defensively\n- Creates potential threats that Black must address immediately\n\nAnswer: R: d8-g8"}
