ason: I choose **N: c3-d5** because it places my knight on a superb central outpost where it controls critical squares (c7, e7, b6, f6), supports potential invasion plans, and keeps maximum flexibility for coordinating with my rook. From d5, the knight can support various attacking ideas while Black's pieces are somewhat uncoordinated. This is more dynamic than simply capturing the e4 pawn.\n\nAnswer: N: c3-d5"}
