ve. It gives check, forcing the Black King to move to a worse square. After the King moves, my Rook controls the 7th rank, cutting off the King from defending the pawns and creating mating threats. In Rook endgames, the 7th rank is often decisive as it attacks pawns and restricts the enemy King. This move maintains maximum pressure and improves my position significantly.\n\nAnswer: R: f8-f7"}
