orse square (likely Kg7, Kg5, or Kh5). This maintains maximum pressure and restricts Black's options. Keeping the rook active and the Black king under constant pressure is key in rook endgames. After Kg7 or Kh7, I can continue to dominate with my rook while advancing my pawns. If Kg5 or Kh5, the king moves toward the center but becomes more vulnerable to checks and my advancing pawns.\n\nAnswer: R: f7-f6"}
