mediately\n2. The queen on e4 controls a central position\n3. After the king moves (likely to f5, f3, g5, or g3), I can continue restricting its movement\n4. This begins the systematic process of driving the king to the edge for checkmate\n5. Direct forcing moves are most efficient in won endgames\n\n**Answer:** Q: e8-e4"}
